W. The verified artifact (Paper 017) — 1.2.206-1.2.222:
AlphaProof Code; the specification as the trusted
artifact; testing a specification; the amendment
protocol; the prover team; the gatekeeper; a formal
semantics of an instruction set; hooks; verification
at the machine-code level; the binary implements the
model; the concretization homomorphism; refinement up
to collisions; reductions as priced programs; PQXDH;
the Triple Ratchet; a key used twice, judged together;
the trusted base, enumerated.
The cluster calls at the founding: cluster Q SUPPORTED
and put to work — its engine and its kernel floor
carry a deployment-grade campaign, and the seat of the human moves from prover to the one who states; the translation
pole of cluster G made into a pair of poles, the
rider standing on 1.2.48; cluster F SUPPORTED — its
floor is here the acceptance test itself; cluster B
SUPPORTED as kin — the harness grown to a crew, with
a gate the harnesses of cluster U lacked; and Q84, the
open question of cluster V, is pressed by a worked
neighbour — the gatekeeper prevents wrong acceptance
as the bench prevents illegal moves — pressed, not
closed. Links outward: 1.2.210 to 1.2.15 (the
harness); 1.2.211 to 1.2.41 (the floor); 1.2.214 to
1.2.48 and to the foundation 1.3.213; 1.2.222 to the
standing record (1.4.1-1.4.6). Restructure Pass #11
