Y. The dual, computed (Paper 019) — 1.2.237-1.2.247:
the joint numerical range; the determinantal
polynomial; the algebraic Kippenhahn
variety; Katz's test; the Gauss map; sampling the
dual; the candidate degree; completely split primes;
reconstruction across the roots; certification of the
reconstruction; the four certified dual surfaces. The centre of gravity of the cluster is its own: a classical
object of matrix analysis — the range and its
generating dual — made computable by sampling and
interpolation in place of the older striking-out road, every output
carrying an exact certificate. The calls at the
founding: cluster E NEIGHBOUR — projective duality
and determinantal surfaces stand near the algebraic ground of the annex, and the author's own trade is the
computational study of surfaces of the kind the annex holds;
but nothing here is symplectic, no manifold is glued
or counted, and the machinery — sampling, kernels,
lifts — belongs to E in no part. Cluster W KIN IN SHAPE —
a computed object admitted only through an exact
gate, its certification cost printed in the open;
the kinship is recorded at 1.2.246 and priced as
shape, the gate here being the object itself, not a
held-out statement. Cluster Q NEIGHBOUR AT A
DISTANCE — both clusters compute with algebra in
systems (Magma and Singular here; Lean there), and
share nothing else. Links outward: 1.2.246 to
1.2.211 (the gatekeeper); 1.2.237 to 1.2.14 (the
measurement agenda). Restructure Pass #12 fell due
