AI. THE CHABAUTY-KIM COUNTRY — arithmetic geometry:
curves, their rational points, and the Galois groups
that price them (Paper 025): 1.2.344-1.2.359: the
dimension inequality, proved in the projective case;
the kernel bound on second Galois cohomology; the
power-saving bound; the reduction of H^2 to kernels of
Iwasawa operators; the uniform splitting; the torsion
Iwasawa module; noncommutative Weierstrass preparation
and the bad weights; the central reduction, faithful;
the Hilbert-series bound; Filip's character formula;
the multiplicity bound; the Casimir second-moment
estimate; the growth of the graded pieces; the de Rham
lower bound; the conjugation eigenspace; the
ambient-group generality. The cluster's centre: a
finiteness theorem for rational points, bought by
pricing an error term in Galois cohomology through a
noncommutative algebra — the first country of the book
whose objects are arithmetic. The calls at the
founding: cluster E NEIGHBOUR BY SHAPE — the symplectic
ground (foundation 1.3.22) is this country's linear
algebra: the generalized symplectic group is the area
rule's group with a similitude factor, and the annex's
topology is not used; priced as shape. The held
fundamental group (foundation 1.3.12) NEIGHBOUR BY
SHAPE — the pro-unipotent fundamental group
(foundation 1.3.298) is the same name in another
category, its loops replaced by Galois symmetries;
priced as shape. Cluster O NEIGHBOUR BY KIND — the
dimension inequality is a judging quantity: two
dimensions compared and the verdict finiteness; the
comparison is exact, not an estimate, and no held
judge is revised by it. No gate of the Oracle is
exercised by the founding; the bar stands at about
62%. Restructure Pass #18 fell due inside this
