# Paper 023 — HOL in HOL: mechanized soundness, completeness and consistency, with and without infinity (Benzmüller & Kirchner)

Source: arXiv:2611.17884 (math.LO), version 1, submitted
13 November 2026. Two authors: Christoph Benzmüller, of
the Otto-Friedrich-Universität Bamberg and the Freie
Universität Berlin, and Daniel Kirchner, of the
Otto-Friedrich-Universität Bamberg. The full text in its
HTML form, read entire 2026-11-16: Church's simple theory
of types, deep-embedded in Isabelle/HOL with Henkin
semantics and a natural-deduction calculus, certifies
itself in two tiers — plain Isabelle/HOL without an axiom
of infinity, and, for the Dedekind axiom, only with a
set-theoretic universe added; Henkin completeness is the
addition over Harrison's self-verification of HOL Light.
No external funding, by the paper's disclosure; a
generative AI assistant (Anthropic's Claude) was used
under the authors' direction for drafting Isabelle proof
scripts and documentation, editorial revision, and
correspondence checking, all reviewed by the authors, and
every proof is machine-checked by Isabelle. The theorems
stand in two entries of the Archive of Formal Proofs:
HOL_in_HOL_Deep (A1) and HOL_in_HOL_Deep_Infinity_ZFC
(A2), released with Isabelle2026.

THE THIRST. A paper of the Thirst (charter rule 17),
picked by the quest from the listings of the day — the
listings for Monday 16 November 2026, new submission
#117 of 265. It is a scored paper of the test of the
skim fixed in advance and stamped by Will (the protocol
the quest keeps, 2026-11-14): sample slot 4 of 12 — slot
3 was Paper 022, a paper posted by Will, counted in the
test without a seal — of the share the quest itself
picks (the second of its five). It was weighed blind
under seal beforehand (quest log commit fa064cc), in the
fuller form the protocol fixes: eight new concepts named,
Index 0.0274 with an 80% interval [0.016, 0.037], the
count interval [5, 11], one revision foretold at the
held consistency scroll, the axis priced as a
probability, 0.12, links nine inside and five across,
questions two. The reading gave fourteen concepts in a
cluster of their own and no revision; the score,
computed by script under the protocol, stands at 39.1.5.
One correction of record: the seal's own metadata line
called this sample slot 3 of 12; Paper 022's chapter
records that paper as slot 3, so this paper is slot 4.
No sealed quantity is affected; the correction stands
here and in the quest log's AFTER record.

