# Paper 023 — synthesis: the certifier priced by its own strength [synthesis]

[synthesis] The tracker has held kernels since its
first week: one small trusted checker (1.2.41), and
consistency as the empty claim staying empty (1.2.47).
What it had never priced is the strength of the hands
doing the certifying. This paper draws that line inside
a single system and finds it is not where a casual
reading would put it: completeness — the strongest
sounding property — is cheap, a first-tier theorem,
while one consistency statement, for one axiom with no
finite model, is what costs a universe. The shape
rhymes with the tracker's own keeping: the MVO registry
is proved accurate by a Lean model whose honesty
boundary is stated in the areas — Lean proves the
bookkeeping, not worldly truth. Paper 023 is that
honesty boundary, drawn by a paper, for a logic: a
certificate states not only what was certified, but in
what strength the certifier stood when it signed.
[synthesis] And the audit is the transferable part.
The footprint discipline — instantiate the claim at the
smallest types, walk the proof terms, name the four
places the forbidden principle actually enters — is a
way of pricing any 'proved without X' claim, including
the claims this tracker files about itself. The skim's
failure on this paper belongs in the same paragraph:
it priced the spine of the founding and missed its
furniture, because an abstract lists results, and a
founding's count lives in its instruments — the audit,
the two interfaces, the rank measure — which an
abstract names only in passing, if at all.
# Paper 023 — Open questions Q120-Q122

Q120 — the minimality of the Harrison-style interface.
Is the encoded-power assumption (Sm_pow) of
harrison_universe (1.2.314) necessary for full function
spaces, or can the construction of hol_universe
(1.2.313) be carried on less? The paper leaves the
exact cardinal content of its seven assumptions open,
and claims no minimality. (Opened by Paper 023,
section 12.)

Q121 — the Gödel step, formalized. Step (4) of the
carrier-obstruction argument (1.2.311) — the appeal to
Gödel's second incompleteness theorem — is discussed,
not formalized. Can the equiconsistency of
Isabelle/HOL's monomorphic core with NK plus infinity
and choice be formalized in its own right, with enough
arithmetic interpreted inside NK with DInf (Dedekind's
own theorem, that the axiom yields a model of the Peano
axioms, as the first derivation), and Paulson's
mechanized incompleteness theorems as the model to
follow? (Opened by Paper 023, sections 4 and 12.)

Q122 — the boundary, drawn for a dependent logic. The
paper's object logic is also the base of dependently
typed HOL (DHOL), which erases to HOL soundly and
completely for provability, and Rabe's lax models for
DHOL come with soundness and completeness of their own.
Do the two interfaces of this paper connect to a
formalization of DHOL semantics, and does the tier
boundary (1.2.304) fall at the same place — between the
sentences with finite models and the sentences without?
(Open question the paper itself names as the natural
first candidate for reuse; opened by Paper 023,
sections 11 and 12.)
