# Study S015 — the house reading [synthesis]

AN ALGORITHM WITH A RECEIPT SHAPE THE HOUSE RECOGNIZES.
The artifact of the study arrives with the two receipts
this house trusts most, already in its hands: its parts
are priced one at a time (the ablation at 40.1.3), and
its whole is priced on ground its making never touched
(the unseen suite). That is the shape of the fair shake
of Chapter 37 turned outward: a claim whose parts carry
prices, tested where its maker did not tune it. The one
receipt it cannot hand itself is the outside run — and
the house's own spot-check at 40.1.3 is a first, small
one: the artifact stands up in another house's hands, on
one configuration, at +6.40% on mean with a seed against
it. [synthesis]

THE QUESTIONS THE STUDY LEAVES ON THE HOUSE'S OWN DESK.
Q124 — the price of the baseline. Every gain in the
chapter is priced against e-means, and e-means' own
headline — Lloyd's 25-epoch loss met in 1.4 to 2.6
epochs — stands on its authors' runs: a re-writing by a
third party of its published update rule, in the days
after its release, measured 1.5x where the paper's shape
promises ten, and found the revival the component the
toy case turns on. If the price of the baseline moves,
every relative price in this cluster moves with it.
Which of the numbers of the chapter are facts about
s-means, and which are facts about the distance between
two sets of authors' runs? [synthesis]
Q125 — the guard or the search. The judge of the
evolution was guarded — a worst-case penalty, parity of
time and memory, no extra epochs — and the artifact it
produced generalizes. The house's own practice would
credit the guards before the search: a guarded judge is
a specification, and cluster I (1.2.57-1.2.64) is the
book's standing account of what a specification buys.
Would a hand-written revision of e-means, built under
the same guards and priced by the same suite, stand
where the evolved one stands? Until that control is run,
the chapter prices the pair — search plus guard — and
cannot price either alone. [synthesis]
Q126 — the silent round. The search ended when one round
rejected all four of its candidates, and the artifact of
that moment is v8. One silent round is a thin signal to
end on: what would a second silent round have cost, and
what would it have bought — the same artifact at a
higher price of search, or a different one? The tracker
has met the shape before, in its own stopping rules; it
stands open here on the machine of the study itself
(1.5.2). [synthesis]

THE MIRROR FOR THE TRACKER ITSELF.
The tracker prices its own skim the way this study
prices its artifact: a frozen instrument, judged on work
arriving after its own tuning, its parts priced by what
their removal costs. The study is the first in the book
whose method is the tracker's own method wearing the
clothes of another field — evolution over a graph of
parts, under a judge with guards, is the delta rule's
discipline with the roles turned: the model proposes,
the record decides. [synthesis]
